<section class="source-band" aria-labelledby="progress-heading">
  <div class="section-inner band-grid">
    <div>
      <p class="section-label">Dossier method</p>
      <h2 id="progress-heading">Small signals enter the archive in sequence.</h2>
    </div>
    <ol class="progression-list">
      <li class="complete">
        <span>01</span>
        <h3>Spark</h3>
        <p>A short post, image, object, joke, field observation, or cursed moment catches the signal before it disappears.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="complete">
        <span>02</span>
        <h3>Trace</h3>
        <p>Caption, alt text, tags, timestamp, and first context give the signal enough handles to survive.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="active">
        <span>03</span>
        <h3>Entry</h3>
        <p>The FI entry stabilizes the specimen: what appeared, what was observed, what remains uncertain, and why it was kept.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span>04</span>
        <h3>Dossier</h3>
        <p>The case file examines the object as evidence without rushing it into a finished interpretation.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span>05</span>
        <h3>Doctrine</h3>
        <p>The final abstraction names the principle revealed through the artifact while leaving the artifact intact.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span>06</span>
        <h3>Return</h3>
        <p>The doctrine points back to the shelf so future records can enter the same chain cleanly.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

